{"id":"PHM","name":"Philemon","chapters":[{"number":1,"verses":[{"number":1,"text":"Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, To Philemon our beloved fellow worker,","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":46,"end":49,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":2,"text":"to Apphia our sister, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets at your house:","notes":[{"at":91,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"1:2 You and Your are singular throughout this letter, except in verses 3, 22, and 25.","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["1:2 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["You "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["and "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["Your "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["are singular throughout this letter, except in verses 3, 22, and 25."]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":73,"end":83,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":3,"text":"Grace and peace to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":47,"end":50,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":4,"text":"I always thank my God, remembering you in my prayers,","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":5,"text":"because I hear about your faith in the Lord Jesus and your love for all the saints.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":6,"text":"I pray that your partnership in the faith may become effective as you fully acknowledge every good thing that is ours in Christ.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":0,"end":6,"marker":"add"},{"start":99,"end":104,"marker":"add"},{"start":110,"end":112,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":7,"text":"I take great joy and encouragement in your love, because you, brother, have refreshed the hearts of the saints.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":8,"text":"So although in Christ I am bold enough to order you to do what is proper,","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":3,"end":11,"marker":"add"},{"start":52,"end":57,"marker":"add"},{"start":63,"end":65,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":9,"text":"I prefer to appeal on the basis of love. For I, Paul, am now aged, and a prisoner of Christ Jesus as well.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":41,"end":44,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":10,"text":"I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whose father I became while I was in chains.","notes":[{"at":38,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"1:10 Onesimus means useful (see verse 11) or beneficial (see verse 20).","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["1:10 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["Onesimus "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["means "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["useful "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["(see verse 11) or "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["beneficial "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["(see verse 20)."]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":61,"end":72,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":11,"text":"Formerly he was useless to you, but now he has become useful both to you and to me.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":9,"end":15,"marker":"add"},{"start":40,"end":53,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":12,"text":"I am sending back to you him who is my very heart.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":13,"text":"I would have liked to keep him with me, so that on your behalf he could minister to me in my chains for the gospel.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":27,"end":30,"marker":"add"},{"start":90,"end":92,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":14,"text":"But I did not want to do anything without your consent, so that your goodness will not be out of compulsion, but by your own free will.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":10,"end":13,"marker":"add"},{"start":25,"end":33,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":15,"text":"For perhaps this is why he was separated from you for a while, so that you might have him back for good —","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":41,"end":49,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":16,"text":"no longer as a slave, but better than a slave, as a beloved brother. He is especially beloved  to me, but even more so to you, both in person and in the Lord.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":47,"end":49,"marker":"add"},{"start":69,"end":74,"marker":"add"},{"start":86,"end":94,"marker":"add"},{"start":149,"end":152,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":17,"text":"So if you consider me a partner, receive him as you would receive me.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":48,"end":65,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":18,"text":"But if he has wronged you in any way or owes you anything, charge it to my account.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":45,"end":57,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":19,"text":"I, Paul, write this with my own hand. I will repay it— not to mention that you owe me your very self.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":15,"end":19,"marker":"add"},{"start":51,"end":53,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":20,"text":"Yes, brother, let me have some benefit from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in Christ.","notes":[{"at":38,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"1:20 Greek onaimēn, a play on the name Onesimus","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["1:20 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["Greek "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["onaimēn"]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":[", a play on the name "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["Onesimus"]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":51,"end":54,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":21,"text":"Confident of your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even more than I ask.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":22,"text":"In the meantime, prepare a guest room for me, because I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":23,"text":"Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, sends you greetings,","notes":[],"characterSpans":[]},{"number":24,"text":"as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers.","notes":[],"characterSpans":[{"start":0,"end":5,"marker":"add"},{"start":32,"end":35,"marker":"add"}]},{"number":25,"text":"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit.","notes":[{"at":55,"marker":"f","caller":"+","text":"1:25 BYZ and TR include Amen.","content":[{"type":"char","marker":"fr","content":["1:25 "]},{"type":"char","marker":"ft","content":["BYZ and TR include "]},{"type":"char","marker":"fqa","content":["Amen."]}]}],"characterSpans":[{"start":35,"end":37,"marker":"add"}]}],"headings":[{"afterVerse":null,"style":"s1","text":"Greetings from Paul and Timothy","content":["Greetings from Paul and Timothy"]},{"afterVerse":null,"style":"r","text":"(Philippians 1:1–2; Colossians 1:1–2)","content":["(",{"type":"ref","loc":"PHP 1:1-2","content":["Philippians 1:1–2"]},"; ",{"type":"ref","loc":"COL 1:1-2","content":["Colossians 1:1–2"]},")"]},{"afterVerse":3,"style":"s1","text":"Philemon’s Faith and Love","content":["Philemon’s Faith and Love"]},{"afterVerse":7,"style":"s1","text":"Paul’s Appeal for Onesimus","content":["Paul’s Appeal for Onesimus"]},{"afterVerse":22,"style":"s1","text":"Additional Greetings","content":["Additional Greetings"]}],"paragraphs":[{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":0,"end":58}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":1,"start":59,"end":97},{"verse":2,"start":0,"end":98}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":2,"start":98,"end":98},{"verse":3,"start":0,"end":69}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":3,"start":69,"end":69},{"verse":4,"start":0,"end":53},{"verse":5,"start":0,"end":83},{"verse":6,"start":0,"end":128},{"verse":7,"start":0,"end":111}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":7,"start":111,"end":111},{"verse":8,"start":0,"end":73},{"verse":9,"start":0,"end":106}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":9,"start":106,"end":106},{"verse":10,"start":0,"end":83},{"verse":11,"start":0,"end":83},{"verse":12,"start":0,"end":50}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":12,"start":50,"end":50},{"verse":13,"start":0,"end":115},{"verse":14,"start":0,"end":135},{"verse":15,"start":0,"end":105},{"verse":16,"start":0,"end":158}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":16,"start":158,"end":158},{"verse":17,"start":0,"end":69},{"verse":18,"start":0,"end":83},{"verse":19,"start":0,"end":101}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":19,"start":101,"end":101},{"verse":20,"start":0,"end":88}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":20,"start":88,"end":88},{"verse":21,"start":0,"end":91}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":21,"start":91,"end":91},{"verse":22,"start":0,"end":113}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":22,"start":113,"end":113},{"verse":23,"start":0,"end":66},{"verse":24,"start":0,"end":60}]},{"style":"p","spans":[{"verse":24,"start":60,"end":60},{"verse":25,"start":0,"end":55}]}],"offsetUnit":"unicode-codepoint"}],"frontMatter":[{"style":"h","text":"Philemon","content":["Philemon"]},{"style":"toc1","text":"Philemon","content":["Philemon"]},{"style":"toc2","text":"Philemon","content":["Philemon"]},{"style":"toc3","text":"PHM","content":["PHM"]},{"style":"mt1","text":"Philemon","content":["Philemon"]}]}
